ressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IRIE MITSUHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ISHII NOBUAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAMA MICHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WADA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IRIE, MITSUHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHII, NOBUAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIGUCHI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAMA, MICHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>(1) A cosmetic preparation containing silica-coated metal oxide particles whose surface has been treated with a hydrophobizing agent; (2) particles obtained by treating metal oxide particles having a specific ratio regarding infrared absorption spectrum intensity and a specific refractive index with a hydrophobizing agent, and a process for producing the particles; and a sol of a silica-coated metal oxide from which the particles are obtained, and a process for producing the sol. An ultraviolet-screening cosmetic preparation giving an excellent feeling of transparency can be obtained in which the particles are satisfactorily dispersed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne (1) une préparation cosmétique contenant des particules d'oxyde métallique enrobées de silice dont les surfaces ont été traitées avec un agent qui leur confère des qualités hydrophobes, (2) des particules obtenues par traitement de particules d'oxyde métallique présentant une valeur spécifique d'intensité d'absorption dans l'infrarouge et un indice de réfraction spécifique avec un agent conférant une qualité hydrophobe, ainsi qu'un procédé permettant de produire ces particules, un oxyde métallique revêtu d'un sol de silice, à partir duquel ces particules sont formées, et un procédé permettant de préparer ce sol. On peut obtenir ainsi une préparation cosmétique formant un écran contre les ultraviolet, donnant une impression de transparence appréciable et dans laquelle les particules sont dispersées de manière satisfaisante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>